WEBVTT

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:03.480
Kusakabe-san.

00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:07.490
It's not like we came to you on a whim.

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:10.810
Please give it some serious
thought before you decide.

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:49.460
What do we do?
The competition is only one week away!

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:51.390
Bit late to be saying that, don't you think?

00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:54.250
I have to practise more.

00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:56.400
Hear me, every living being in this world!

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:58.840
Share your energy with me!

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:00.510
But you have more than you'll ever need.

00:02:01.030 --> 00:02:03.020
Ask for musical ability instead.

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:04.350
<i>You're</i> asking for a kicking.

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:07.690
See you later, then.
We'll be awaiting your reply.

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:13.270
You were still practising?

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:14.370
Yes.

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:17.130
Good work. Be careful on the way home.

00:02:17.130 --> 00:02:17.610
We will!

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:19.110
Want me to return the key for you?

00:02:19.630 --> 00:02:21.320
Thank you.

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:23.130
We'll be on our way, then.

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:24.040
Let's go, Chika-chan.

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:25.490
Good-bye!

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:29.640
Wait, where are we going?

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:30.990
Follow my lead.

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:32.860
Who knows?

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:37.420
You're from the Hamamatsu Symphony, right?

00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:39.450
Y-Yeah.

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:40.590
And you are?

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:43.450
We're huge fans of yours!

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:44.070
Right?

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:46.260
Uh, right!

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:47.720
Thank you.

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:54.290
We've been hoping to see our advisor,
Kusakabe-sensei, conduct such an orchestra.

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:56.950
What brought you here today?

00:02:56.950 --> 00:02:58.160
That's exactly why, actually—

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:00.290
I'm afraid we can't talk about it just yet.

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:02.160
Not until it's officially decided.

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:04.780
Anyway, best of luck.

00:03:10.050 --> 00:03:11.250
What was that all about?

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:14.710
They came here to recruit Kusakabe-sensei.

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:19.050
I saw the envelope he was holding
and the licence plate of the car

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:20.700
and decided to bluff.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:22.720
Their reaction told the whole story.

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:25.930
They asked Sensei to be their conductor.

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:28.630
But Sensei...

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:34.360
He wouldn't abandon us and leave, right?

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:35.480
I'm not so sure.

00:03:36.310 --> 00:03:39.550
If Sensei seriously wants to
go back to the music world,

00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:41.950
this should be an opportunity like no other.

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:47.950
But aren't we all aiming to make it to Fumon Hall
in the Category A All-Japans next year?

00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:49.750
That's my aim too, but...

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:52.750
Homura-san.

00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:54.940
You're not focusing.

00:03:54.940 --> 00:03:56.540
Oh, sorry.

00:03:56.940 --> 00:03:58.040
Want to call it a day?

00:03:58.560 --> 00:03:59.630
No, I'll keep going!

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:03.260
Serizawa-san...

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:06.090
How are we right now?

00:04:06.950 --> 00:04:08.050
What do you mean?

00:04:08.050 --> 00:04:16.350
How do we look in the eyes of a long-time
musician, like you or Kusakabe-sensei?

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:18.320
Can you handle the truth?

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:20.070
Yeah.

00:04:21.770 --> 00:04:25.370
There may have been no
odds-on favourites this year,

00:04:25.370 --> 00:04:28.940
but it's still a mystery how you
made it to the Tokai regionals.

00:04:28.940 --> 00:04:32.600
Your performances are so unbalanced
that they wear the listener out.

00:04:33.820 --> 00:04:35.370
That's not all, though.

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:36.370
Want to hear the rest?

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:38.710
I'll listen until I drop!

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:43.480
Despite all that, Kusakabe-sensei brings
your unbalanced performances together.

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:46.180
And you really know how to make
an impact from the get-go.

00:04:46.730 --> 00:04:49.180
You're fearless thanks to
your time in volleyball.

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:51.880
The band lacks both depth and overall skill,

00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:58.100
but it stays afloat because Maren, Narushima-san,
Kamijou-kun, and Kaiyuu are doing their best.

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:03.940
Instead of helping the listener relax,
your performances gently wear them out.

00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:07.160
And making your audience
feel that way counts for a lot.

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:08.780
So hold your head high.

00:05:10.190 --> 00:05:10.890
Okay.

00:05:15.630 --> 00:05:17.460
Narushima-san!

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:19.320
Let's do our best!

00:05:19.320 --> 00:05:20.330
What's with you?

00:05:20.330 --> 00:05:22.480
Apparently Serizawa-san showered us with praise.

00:05:24.230 --> 00:05:26.420
All right. Let's begin rehearsing.

00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:27.750
Okay!

00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:28.760
Okay...

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:32.930
Let's start from the top, then.

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:35.890
The baton broke!

00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:40.270
Everything is fleeting.
If it has shape, it will one day break.

00:05:40.670 --> 00:05:43.070
It could be a bad omen.

00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:46.490
It isn't like you to say such
ominous things, Homura-senpai.

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:47.830
What's gotten into you?

00:05:47.830 --> 00:05:50.960
You're usually so thick you wouldn't
notice a black cat crossing your path,

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:52.990
but now you're way too high-strung.

00:05:52.990 --> 00:05:54.260
I'm sorry.

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:56.000
Oh, Sensei.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:58.120
Shall I stick it back together with rice?

00:05:58.500 --> 00:05:59.580
Rice?

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:01.360
What a crude method.

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:03.040
Sorry I'm crude.

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:05.940
It's all right. I can use my hands to conduct.

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:07.590
Anyway, let's begin rehearsal.

00:06:08.590 --> 00:06:12.320
Come on, Chika-chan. People are going
to find out if you panic like that.

00:06:12.320 --> 00:06:13.810
Sorry.

00:06:13.810 --> 00:06:16.390
We need to focus on practice right now.

00:06:16.390 --> 00:06:18.340
Yeah, you're right.

00:06:19.160 --> 00:06:21.850
I want us to perform as well as we possibly can.

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:24.510
Kamijou-kun, Homura-san.

00:06:24.510 --> 00:06:26.360
If you don't mind,
could you chip in 100 yen each?

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:26.820
Oink.

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:27.400
President...

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:30.020
Did you run out of pocket money for this month?

00:06:30.020 --> 00:06:32.910
I did see you and Haruta
going halfsies on an Umaibo.

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:35.790
That was me graciously sharing with him.

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:37.240
That's not it.

00:06:37.240 --> 00:06:40.460
We're gifting a new baton to Kusakabe-sensei.

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:41.760
To Sensei?

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:45.720
We were already thinking about giving him
something as a token of our gratitude.

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:47.800
And we think this'll make a great present.

00:06:49.670 --> 00:06:52.220
That baton wouldn't suit Kusakabe-sensei.

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:53.560
But it looks so nice!

00:06:53.560 --> 00:06:57.520
Forget about what <i>you</i> want!
Pick something <i>Sensei</i> would want to use!

00:06:57.520 --> 00:06:59.370
What would you know about him?!

00:06:59.370 --> 00:07:01.980
I know I don't trust your awful taste!

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:06.440
I'm glad we found something nice.

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:08.020
I'll hand it to him!

00:07:08.020 --> 00:07:09.020
No, I will!

00:07:09.020 --> 00:07:10.980
As president, I will.

00:07:10.980 --> 00:07:13.280
If you're going to fight about it, I will.

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:17.950
Why don't we let Kae- and Sae-senpai do it?
They're the ones who suggested it.

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:19.790
Me!

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:21.290
Kusakabe-sensei!

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:24.670
I mean, I spotted him.

00:07:25.530 --> 00:07:26.540
It <i>is</i> him.

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:28.840
I thought he took the bus
to and from school every day.

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:30.010
Sensei!

00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:32.920
Homura-san! You'll ruin the surprise!

00:07:32.920 --> 00:07:34.470
Oh, right.

00:07:34.470 --> 00:07:35.860
Be seeing you, then.

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:38.810
I need to see my family today.

00:07:41.930 --> 00:07:42.860
Me too!

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:45.380
See you guys tomorrow!

00:07:45.380 --> 00:07:47.460
They're going to see his family together?

00:07:47.460 --> 00:07:50.030
Are those two dating?!

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:51.190
Who knows?

00:07:53.750 --> 00:07:55.160
You're stealing another march on me?

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:58.870
I knew you'd never go see your
family of your own free will!

00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:03.830
H-Hey!

00:08:05.470 --> 00:08:06.330
What is this?

00:08:06.330 --> 00:08:08.480
It's like we're tailing him.

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:10.480
Awfully perceptive today, aren't we?

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:17.850
Looks like he's changing trains.

00:08:18.320 --> 00:08:20.850
He's probably headed to Hamamatsu.

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:23.650
Hamamatsu... Symphony?!

00:08:30.470 --> 00:08:33.000
What are you planning?

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:36.630
If Sensei's planning to give the
Hamamatsu Symphony his answer,

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:39.470
then I'm going to tell him
how I feel before he does.

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:44.960
I'll say, "Please don't go.
Stay on as our instructor next year too."

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:46.400
Oh.

00:08:46.400 --> 00:08:49.710
This isn't a bad offer for him.

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:55.470
Still, I believed that he'd
decide to stay with us in time.

00:08:55.470 --> 00:08:57.210
I wanted to believe that he would.

00:08:57.880 --> 00:09:02.460
But if I let him leave without
telling him how I feel,

00:09:03.690 --> 00:09:06.480
I know I'll regret it forever.

00:09:07.390 --> 00:09:12.190
But hey, we don't know for sure
that he's going to accept.

00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:16.530
Yeah, but if he was going to refuse,
couldn't he have done it over the phone?

00:09:17.380 --> 00:09:18.780
Right...

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:21.400
Coming up: Tanikawa.

00:09:21.400 --> 00:09:22.620
He's getting off!

00:09:23.470 --> 00:09:25.270
But we're not at Hamamatsu yet.

00:09:25.990 --> 00:09:26.940
This is odd.

00:09:26.940 --> 00:09:29.090
We bought tickets to Hamamatsu!

00:09:29.090 --> 00:09:31.920
Love sure can lead people astray, huh, Chika-chan?

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:32.960
Dude.

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:37.130
I wonder where he's going.

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:40.830
Remember how he arrived late
for the district qualifiers?

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:42.640
Yeah.

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:45.280
On August 1st, the day of the qualifiers,

00:09:45.280 --> 00:09:49.900
service on the Tokaido line was interrupted
for a while due to signal failure.

00:09:50.350 --> 00:09:53.510
He might have come here that day too.

00:09:53.510 --> 00:09:55.530
Maybe that's why he was late.

00:09:55.530 --> 00:10:00.170
Then he's headed to the same
place he went to before?

00:10:00.170 --> 00:10:03.710
Wasn't he in formal wear then?

00:10:03.710 --> 00:10:05.410
He'd taken his jacket off, though.

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:10.080
Maybe he's here today to pick up something
he forgot at a wedding he attended that day?

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:17.170
You remember that whole thing about how Sensei
walked out on the Berliner Symphoniker and disappeared?

00:10:17.170 --> 00:10:18.130
Yeah.

00:10:18.990 --> 00:10:21.470
That was on an August 1st too.

00:10:31.320 --> 00:10:34.080
Taking the same bus would be pushing it, surely.

00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:35.820
Do you have money on you?

00:10:37.690 --> 00:10:39.320
Follow that bus!

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:41.310
As far as you can take us
for 1,000 yen, please.

00:10:41.310 --> 00:10:43.000
We'll lose him!

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:45.220
But what about our tickets home?

00:10:45.220 --> 00:10:47.670
Youth is a one-way trip.

00:10:48.210 --> 00:10:49.030
What.

00:10:57.690 --> 00:10:58.750
Haruta...

00:10:58.750 --> 00:11:00.730
Are you seriously doing this?

00:11:00.730 --> 00:11:01.510
Yeah.

00:11:02.240 --> 00:11:04.300
I'll go and tell him how I feel.

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:09.140
Do you have to put it like that every time?
It makes me nervous.

00:11:19.250 --> 00:11:20.070
Chika-chan?!

00:11:20.070 --> 00:11:21.190
Damn, you're heavy!

00:11:24.310 --> 00:11:25.740
We're sorry!

00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:27.990
No need to apologise.

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:30.080
But why did you come
all the way here?

00:11:31.030 --> 00:11:37.420
We thought you were going to Hamamatsu
to accept the offer to conduct their symphony.

00:11:37.420 --> 00:11:39.290
How did you know about that?

00:11:39.290 --> 00:11:45.440
Well, Haruta realised that those people
were from Hamamatsu Symphony...

00:11:45.940 --> 00:11:47.480
Isn't that right, Haruta?

00:11:47.480 --> 00:11:48.200
Yeah...

00:11:49.380 --> 00:11:51.470
Whenever I'm in doubt,
I find myself coming here...

00:11:52.330 --> 00:11:55.480
and wondering what they would say.

00:11:55.960 --> 00:11:57.120
They?

00:11:58.030 --> 00:11:58.740
Sensei.

00:11:59.460 --> 00:12:00.860
There's no need to hesitate.

00:12:01.490 --> 00:12:04.110
Accept the offer to be conductor.

00:12:05.580 --> 00:12:07.820
Remember what you said before?

00:12:07.820 --> 00:12:12.910
That getting to Fumon Hall is important,
but our lives after that are much more important.

00:12:12.910 --> 00:12:14.800
Shouldn't it be the same for you?

00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:17.840
You don't have to worry about us.

00:12:17.840 --> 00:12:21.780
We'll take gold this year and
go to Fumon Hall next year!

00:12:21.780 --> 00:12:23.160
Right, Chika-chan?

00:12:23.160 --> 00:12:25.570
Yeah. You can count on us.

00:12:28.720 --> 00:12:31.520
I'm going to stay here for a while longer.

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:32.310
Okay.

00:12:38.410 --> 00:12:39.200
Sensei!

00:12:40.710 --> 00:12:41.610
Sensei...

00:12:42.820 --> 00:12:46.110
To tell you the truth, we both...

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:49.860
have no money to pay for
the train tickets home!

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:55.120
Why didn't you try to stop him?

00:12:55.800 --> 00:12:59.470
I saw the date on the grave he was visiting.

00:13:00.130 --> 00:13:01.580
It was August 1st.

00:13:02.610 --> 00:13:06.260
The day he was supposed to
conduct the Berliner Symphoniker,

00:13:06.260 --> 00:13:08.220
someone dear to him died.

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:11.650
So that's why he couldn't go to the venue?

00:13:11.650 --> 00:13:13.430
There's no way to tell what happened.

00:13:14.350 --> 00:13:18.100
But right now, he's of two minds
whether to take a step forwards or not.

00:13:19.490 --> 00:13:24.770
Will the Tokai regionals be the
last time we perform with him?

00:13:26.570 --> 00:13:28.960
Let's put on a great performance, Haruta.

00:13:33.570 --> 00:13:36.220
We all chipped in to buy this for you.

00:13:36.220 --> 00:13:38.000
Please use it, if you'd like.

00:13:39.950 --> 00:13:41.100
Thank you.

00:13:44.200 --> 00:13:50.220
<i>I joined the concert band back in the
spring of my first year in high school.</i>

00:13:50.220 --> 00:13:52.900
<i>This is the story of the six seasons
that have passed since then.</i>

00:13:52.900 --> 00:13:54.900
<i>A story of miraculous chance encounters,</i>

00:13:54.900 --> 00:13:56.650
<i>unravelled mysteries,</i>

00:13:56.650 --> 00:13:59.930
<i>and the secrets that dwell in people's hearts.</i>

00:14:01.160 --> 00:14:02.610
Now for performance number nine.

00:14:02.610 --> 00:14:06.570
Representing Shizuoka Prefecture,
it's Shimizu Minami High School

00:14:06.570 --> 00:14:08.450
performing their free-choice piece,
"On a Clear Day".

00:14:09.260 --> 00:14:11.810
Their conductor is Kusakabe Shinjirou.

00:14:15.240 --> 00:14:16.290
Best of luck!

00:19:38.070 --> 00:19:39.870
Hello, Mum?

00:19:39.870 --> 00:19:42.820
Listen, we won gold!

00:19:43.390 --> 00:19:46.640
Bronze is a great result in its own right.

00:19:46.640 --> 00:19:50.840
But if those of us with experience
had led from the front...

00:19:52.090 --> 00:19:56.540
Maybe I could've played better
if I hadn't quit for a while.

00:19:56.540 --> 00:19:58.000
Yeah...

00:19:58.000 --> 00:20:00.560
Our concert band used to have
all of five members,

00:20:00.560 --> 00:20:04.130
so I thought I'd be content
just making it this far.

00:20:05.630 --> 00:20:08.840
But it's the end of the line for us!

00:20:10.550 --> 00:20:14.550
I'm disappointed in myself too.
I got nervous on stage.

00:20:18.690 --> 00:20:20.560
You all did your best!

00:20:20.560 --> 00:20:21.440
Gotou-san,

00:20:21.440 --> 00:20:23.190
Narushima-san, Maren,

00:20:23.570 --> 00:20:24.650
and Kaiyuu...

00:20:24.650 --> 00:20:27.700
We all put on the greatest performance
we could have right now!

00:20:27.700 --> 00:20:28.760
Homura?

00:20:28.760 --> 00:20:30.950
Where do you think we are?

00:20:30.950 --> 00:20:35.250
Not the district or prefectural qualifiers,
but the Tokai regionals!

00:20:35.250 --> 00:20:38.290
Isn't it amazing that we're depressed
at taking bronze at such a huge event?

00:20:39.270 --> 00:20:40.270
Yeah.

00:20:40.270 --> 00:20:42.150
You're right.

00:20:43.420 --> 00:20:45.510
I'm counting on you for next year.

00:20:45.510 --> 00:20:48.230
The band will be fine with her around.

00:20:50.780 --> 00:20:51.960
Good work.

00:20:52.390 --> 00:20:53.670
Sensei...

00:20:54.390 --> 00:20:59.180
If possible, we wanted to
take gold as a gift for you.

00:20:59.180 --> 00:21:02.200
We would never have made it
this far without you.

00:21:03.020 --> 00:21:04.360
Thank you so very much.

00:21:05.860 --> 00:21:08.120
You all performed well today.

00:21:08.930 --> 00:21:11.530
It was the perfect culmination
of all your hard work.

00:21:11.530 --> 00:21:15.240
I'm sure some of you aren't
satisfied with how you played.

00:21:15.710 --> 00:21:21.170
But if you're willing to see today as part
of the process rather than its conclusion,

00:21:21.170 --> 00:21:23.750
then I ask you to work with me
again from tomorrow.

00:21:24.330 --> 00:21:26.750
Yes, sir!

00:21:27.670 --> 00:21:29.630
All right. Let's get on the bus.

00:21:29.630 --> 00:21:32.630
Oh, I need to visit the bathroom.

00:21:54.580 --> 00:21:55.620
Chika-chan.

00:21:56.760 --> 00:21:57.860
What?

00:21:58.790 --> 00:22:04.250
We pour in our blood, sweat, and tears,
believing the sky is the limit for us.

00:22:04.250 --> 00:22:06.640
That's a privilege exclusive to youth.

00:22:07.760 --> 00:22:09.720
So if we're upset, we're free to cry.

00:22:11.160 --> 00:22:16.500
Besides, it's thanks to you that we gathered
so many members and got so far.

00:22:16.940 --> 00:22:19.780
It was thanks to your solving all those mysteries.

00:22:19.780 --> 00:22:21.990
All I did was unlock the mysteries themselves.

00:22:21.990 --> 00:22:23.900
You're the one who unlocked
the hearts of everyone involved.

00:22:25.270 --> 00:22:29.930
With your bundles of energy, guts,
shamelessness, and audacity—

00:22:29.930 --> 00:22:32.440
Hey! If you're gonna praise me, do it right!

00:22:32.440 --> 00:22:33.070
Here.

00:22:33.840 --> 00:22:35.000
Jeez...

00:22:38.870 --> 00:22:40.330
Quit moping about.

00:22:40.750 --> 00:22:42.270
This isn't the end.

00:22:42.270 --> 00:22:43.460
Serizawa-san.

00:22:43.920 --> 00:22:46.100
You didn't leave with your aunt?

00:22:47.310 --> 00:22:49.340
I decided to go home with you.

00:22:50.180 --> 00:22:52.740
Why? Did you get into an argument?

00:22:53.950 --> 00:22:55.340
I've made up my mind.

00:22:55.720 --> 00:22:56.840
About what?

00:22:56.840 --> 00:22:59.570
She's saying she'll join the concert band.

00:23:01.350 --> 00:23:02.350
You're so thick.

00:23:02.910 --> 00:23:04.160
Thank you!

00:23:04.160 --> 00:23:04.820
Oh, come on.

00:23:04.820 --> 00:23:06.070
We'll be together forever!

00:23:06.070 --> 00:23:07.830
Forever's pushing it a bit.

00:23:08.310 --> 00:23:10.700
We third-years will be retiring now.

00:23:11.070 --> 00:23:13.320
We entrust all our dreams to you.

00:23:13.790 --> 00:23:17.960
Also, I spoke with Kusakabe-sensei
and decided on the next president.

00:23:17.960 --> 00:23:19.200
The next president?

00:23:19.200 --> 00:23:21.450
Could be you, Homura-senpai!

00:23:22.080 --> 00:23:22.980
Me?!

00:23:22.980 --> 00:23:24.870
I hereby appoint...

00:23:26.210 --> 00:23:27.240
Maren!

00:23:27.240 --> 00:23:27.970
Ma—

00:23:30.380 --> 00:23:32.460
I look forward to continuing to work with you!
